    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite (BUILD SUCCESS, all tests green) passes. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and it now passes along with the build's MapStruct/OpenAPI code generation.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe feature adds a derived, read-only `telephoneDisplay` field alongside the raw E.164 `telephone`. I placed each piece where it belongs and reused existing code:\n\n1. **`Telephones.java`** (the existing telephone-domain helper that already owns country-code knowledge) \u2014 added `public static String toDisplay(String e164)` which splits off the recognised country code and groups the national digits in threes (`+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`). To do this cleanly I extracted a `longestCountryCode(...)` helper that the existing `toE164` length check now shares instead of duplicating the loop, plus a small `groupInThrees(...)` helper. The class became `public` so the mapper can call it \u2014 matching the sibling helpers `CustomerCode`/`IdentityKeys` in that package.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"telephoneDisplay\", ...)` and a one-line `telephoneDisplay(owner)` default that delegates to `Telephones.toDisplay(owner.getTelephone())`. This mirrors exactly how the mapper already derives `displayName`, `initials`, `locality`, etc.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared `telephoneDisplay` as a `readOnly` string on the `Owner` schema (the DTOs are generated from this spec at build time), so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field and MapStruct populates it.\n\nThe raw `telephone` field is untouched and stays in E.164 form; normalization on POST (via `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`/`Telephones.toE164`) already produces the stored `+61412345678`, and the new formatter reads that back for display.",
